---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { legal } from '../data/legal';

/**
 * Privacy policy. Written against the Australian Privacy Principles (Privacy
 * Act 1988), and to carry the disclosures the platforms Tamtree connects to
 * check for when an app is registered:
 *
 *   * Google / YouTube — the YouTube API Services disclosure, links to the
 *     YouTube Terms and the Google Privacy Policy, how to revoke access, and
 *     the Limited Use statement of the Google API Services User Data Policy.
 *   * Meta — data deletion instructions (#data-deletion is the URL to give as
 *     the app's "Data deletion instructions URL").
 *   * TikTok — what is accessed and how to disconnect.
 *
 * Every fact about the website itself is checked against the build: no
 * analytics, no cookies, the theme choice in localStorage (theme-init.js),
 * Google Fonts in <head> (Base.astro), the waitlist form posting to Buttondown
 * (docs/waitlist.md), hosting on our own server at AWS in Sydney
 * (DEPLOYMENT.md), whose access log is Caddy's (deploy/Caddyfile.web).
 *
 * The wording avoids anything gate:copy forbids (licensing, deployment model,
 * pricing), so this page commits to none of them.
 */
const { entity, abn, contactEmail } = legal;
const mail = `mailto:${contactEmail}`;

const sections = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', title: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'what-we-collect', title: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'connected-accounts', title: 'Connected social accounts' },
  { id: 'how-we-use-it', title: 'How we use it' },
  { id: 'sharing', title: 'Who we share it with' },
  { id: 'overseas', title: 'Overseas storage' },
  { id: 'retention', title: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'security', title: 'Security' },
  { id: 'your-rights', title: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'data-deletion', title: 'Deleting your data' },
  { id: 'children', title: 'Children' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact and complaints' },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What Tamtree collects through its website, waitlist and product, including connected YouTube, Facebook, Instagram and TikTok accounts, and how to access or delete it."
  sections={sections}
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal information Tamtree collects, why, and what you can do about
    it. It covers this website ({legal.site.replace('https://', '')}), the waitlist, and the Tamtree
    product, including the social accounts you can connect to it. We handle personal information
    in line with the Australian Privacy Principles in the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth).
  </p>

  <h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Tamtree is operated by {entity} (ABN {abn}) ("Tamtree", "we", "us"). You can reach us about
    anything in this policy at <a href={mail}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>

  <h3>When you visit this website</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No analytics and no cookies.</strong> The site runs no tracking scripts and sets no
      cookies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your theme choice.</strong> If you switch between light and dark mode, the choice is
      stored in your browser's local storage so the site remembers it. It is never sent to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our web server records standard request details (IP address,
      browser user agent, the page requested, and the time) to deliver the site and protect it
      from abuse.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fonts.</strong> The site loads its typefaces from Google Fonts, so your browser sends
      your IP address and user agent to Google when a page loads.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>When you join the waitlist</h3>
  <p>
    We collect your email address and the updates you opt into (for example, launch news or early
    access). The list is held by our email provider, Buttondown. You can unsubscribe from any email
    we send.
  </p>

  <h3>When you use Tamtree</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your name, email address and workspace settings.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your content:</strong> the workflows you build, the files and media they produce, and
      the run history Tamtree keeps so you can inspect and retry them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Credentials you connect:</strong> API keys and access tokens for the services your
      workflows use. They are encrypted before they are stored, and every time one is read it is
      recorded in an audit log.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Operational data:</strong> logs and error reports needed to run, secure and fix the
      service.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>When you email us,</strong> we keep your message and address to reply.
  </p>

  <h2 id="connected-accounts">Connected social accounts</h2>
  <p>
    Tamtree can upload videos your workflows produce to YouTube, Facebook, Instagram and TikTok. You
    connect each account yourself, using a developer app you create on that platform. Tamtree uses
    what a connection gives it <strong>only to upload the videos you direct it to</strong>. It does
    not read your feed, messages, followers or analytics. It does not use platform data for
    advertising, does not sell it, and does not use it to train AI models.
  </p>

  <h3>YouTube</h3>
  <p>
    Tamtree uses YouTube API Services. When you connect a YouTube channel, Tamtree receives an
    access token for the permissions you approve: uploading videos, and reading your channel's basic
    details to confirm which channel is connected. It stores the token, encrypted, and the details
    of videos it has uploaded for you.
  </p>
  <p>
    By connecting YouTube you agree to the{' '}
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>, and
    Google's handling of your data is described in the{' '}
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>. You can
    revoke Tamtree's access at any time from your{' '}
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">Google Account permissions
    page</a>, as well as by deleting the credential in Tamtree.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tamtree's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the{' '}
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener"
      >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
    >, including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <h3>Facebook and Instagram</h3>
  <p>
    When you connect Meta, Tamtree stores the access token you provide and your Facebook Page ID,
    and looks up the Instagram professional account linked to that Page. It uses them only to
    upload Reels to that Page and account. To remove Tamtree's access on Meta's side, remove the
    app from your Business settings, or from <em>Settings › Business integrations</em> on Facebook.
  </p>

  <h3>TikTok</h3>
  <p>
    When you connect TikTok, Tamtree receives an access token for the permissions you approve:
    your basic account details, and sending videos to your TikTok inbox. Videos arrive as drafts
    that you post yourself. You can disconnect Tamtree in the TikTok app under{' '}
    <em>Settings and privacy › Security › Apps and services</em>, as well as by deleting the
    credential in Tamtree.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-we-use-it">How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide Tamtree: run your workflows, store your content, and do what you ask of it.</li>
    <li>To send the emails you signed up for, and service messages about your account.</li>
    <li>To keep the service secure, prevent abuse, and fix problems.</li>
    <li>To answer you when you contact us.</li>
    <li>To meet our legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal information, and we do not use it for third-party advertising.</p>

  <h2 id="sharing">Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share personal information only as needed to run Tamtree:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Amazon Web Services</strong>, which provides the server this website runs on, in
      Sydney, Australia.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Buttondown</strong>, which holds the waitlist and sends our emails.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong>, which serves the website's typefaces.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>The platforms you connect</strong> (YouTube, Meta, TikTok and others). We send them
      what is needed to carry out your request, such as the video and its title or caption.
    </li>
    <li>
      Infrastructure providers that run the Tamtree service on our behalf, under contracts that
      limit how they may use the data.
    </li>
    <li>Anyone we are required to share it with by law, or to protect people or the service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="overseas">Overseas storage</h2>
  <p>
    Some of our providers, including Buttondown and Google, store or process data outside
    Australia, mainly in the United States. We choose providers that protect personal information
    to a standard comparable to the Australian Privacy Principles.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Waitlist:</strong> until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Account data and content:</strong> while your account is active, then deleted within
      90 days of closing it, unless the law requires us to keep it longer.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Connected-account tokens:</strong> until you delete the credential or close your
      account. They are deleted immediately.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Server and security logs:</strong> for a limited period, usually no more than 90 days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <p>
    We protect personal information with encryption in transit and at rest, access controls and
    audit logging. Credentials and tokens are encrypted with keys kept separate for each workspace.
    No system is perfectly secure. If a data breach is likely to cause you serious harm, we will
    tell you and the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner, as the Notifiable Data
    Breaches scheme requires.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>give you a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
    <li>correct information that is wrong or out of date;</li>
    <li>delete your information;</li>
    <li>stop sending you emails, using the unsubscribe link in any of them.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Email <a href={mail}>{contactEmail}</a>. We will respond within 30 days. Depending on where you
    live, for example the European Union, the United Kingdom or California, you may have further
    rights, such as data portability or objecting to certain processing, and we will honour them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="data-deletion">Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Step-by-step instructions for each platform, and what happens after you ask, are on the{' '}
    <a href="/data-deletion/">data deletion</a> page. In short:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>A connected account</strong> (YouTube, Facebook, Instagram, TikTok): in Tamtree, open{' '}
      <em>Credentials</em> and delete the credential. Its tokens are deleted immediately. Also
      remove Tamtree's access on the platform itself, as described under{' '}
      <a href="#connected-accounts">Connected social accounts</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your account and everything in it:</strong> email <a href={mail}>{contactEmail}</a>{' '}
      from the address on the account, asking us to delete it. We confirm within 7 days and
      complete the deletion within 30.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The waitlist:</strong> use the unsubscribe link in any email, or email us to be
      removed entirely.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Deleting data in Tamtree does not delete videos already published on a platform. Remove those
    on the platform itself.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    Tamtree is a tool for businesses and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect
    personal information from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has given us their
    information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page when our practices change, and change the date at the top. If a change
    is significant, we will tell waitlist members and account holders by email before it takes
    effect.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact and complaints</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, requests and complaints go to <a href={mail}>{contactEmail}</a>. We will respond
    within 30 days. If you are not satisfied with our response, you can complain to the{' '}
    <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints" rel="noopener"
      >Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a
    >.
  </p>
</Legal>
